          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.234,
            0.139,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.292,
            0.233,
            0.538,
            0.252
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "x ^ { 2 } + 1 4 x + 4 9 + x ^ { 2 } = 1 6 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.259,
            0.14,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.258,
            0.518,
            0.277
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "2x^{2} + 14x - 120 = 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.284,
            0.719,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { S o } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the distance "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ } ^ { \\circ } x ^ { \\flat }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the pole from gate B satisfies the equation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.309,
            0.517,
            0.327
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "x^{2}+7x-60=0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.334,
            0.899,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { S o } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " it would be possible to place the pole if this equation has real roots. To see if this is so or not, let us consider its discriminant. The discriminant is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.378,
            0.58,
            0.397
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "b^{2}-4ac=7^{2}-4\\times 1\\times (-60)=289>0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.404,
            0.9,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the given quadratic equation has two real roots, and it is possible to erect the pole on the boundary of the park."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.448,
            0.902,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solving the quadratic equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x^{2}+7x-60=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , by the quadratic formula, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.48,
            0.726,
            0.525
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "x = \\frac{- 7 \\pm \\sqrt{289}}{2} = \\frac{- 7 \\pm 17}{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.527,
            0.339,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 5 \\mathrm { o r } - 1 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.553,
            0.898,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since x is the distance between the pole and the gate B, it must be positive. Therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = - 1 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " will have to be ignored. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { S o } , x   =   5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.601,
            0.899,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the pole has to be erected on the boundary of the park at a distance of 5m from the gate B and 12m from the gate A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.658,
            0.9,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 9 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the discriminant of the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3x^{2}-2x+\\frac{1}{3}=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and hence find the nature of its roots. Find them, if they are real."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.724,
            0.504,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 3,   b = -2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c   =   \\frac { 1 } { 3 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.775,
            0.732,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, discriminant "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b^{2}-4ac=(-2)^{2}-4\\times 3\\times \\frac{1}{3}=4-4=0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.824,
            0.684,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, the given quadratic equation has two equal real roots."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.856,
            0.558,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The roots are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{-b}{2a}, \\frac{-b}{2a}, \\text { i.e., } \\frac{2}{6}, \\frac{2}{6}, \\text { i.e., } \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{3}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
